# This project does not use a local .env file for runtime secrets.
#
# The Cloudflare Worker reads three encrypted secrets at runtime, set with
# `npm run cf:secrets` (or the Cloudflare dashboard):
#
#   OPENAI_API_KEY   Your OpenAI API key (used server-side only).
#   APP_PASSWORD     The single-user login password for this app.
#   SESSION_SECRET   A long random string used as the HMAC key for session
#                     tokens, IP hashes, and the constant-time password check.
#
# Do not put real values in this file or commit them anywhere. Generate
# SESSION_SECRET with something like:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(48).toString('hex'))"
